'''Hisbanya Station''' ({{Lang-bl|Estación de Hisbanya}}) is a major [[W:Railway station|railway station]] in the [[Hisbanya]] borough of the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. It is managed by [[Compañía d'a Estación Confederales|Compañía d'Estación Confederales]]. It serves as the main station for northwestern Castejón, with [[Coruxón station|Coruxón]] serving as the central station for south and southwest Castejón.  

Together with [[Callejón Station|Callejón]] and Coruxón it is one of the three high-speed rail stations within the Metropolis, and it serves the [[Porciúncula–Jatiel high-speed rail line|Porciúncula–Castejón–Jatiel high-speed rail line]], along with the conventional [[Cisalpujarra railway|''Cisalpujarra'']] and ''[[North Ethiopian Railway|Etiopik Norte]]'' railways. It is a major public transport hub, with connections to [[Sol station|dedicated platforms]] on [[Castejón Metro]] lines [[Castejón Metro Casas Viejas Line|1]], [[Castejón Metro Iznájar Line|6]], [[Castejón Metro Maristán Line|8]] and [[Castejón Metro Ferreyra Line|12]], as well as a bus terminal. 

